  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116038",
      "title": "Providing Services via the Element Injector",
      "lectureOrder": 184,
      "videoOrder": 176,
      "sourceHash": "0acd69aa9f7d8e336527a110d52e8140495d320d2d8b85eb47909d909865be3f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 3.81,
          "en": "Now besides providing a service like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.81,
          "end": 7.62,
          "en": "or with help of this configuration object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.62,
          "end": 9.42,
          "en": "there also is another way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.42,
          "end": 13.74,
          "en": "of registering an injectable value with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.74,
          "end": 17.79,
          "en": "You can register it with the element injector instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.79,
          "end": 21.18,
          "en": "of that root environment injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.18,
          "end": 24.78,
          "en": "And the element injector is a special kind of injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 28.8,
          "en": "that's closely tied to your DOM elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 33.48,
          "en": "to your components and directives in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.48,
          "end": 36.69,
          "en": "So if you wanna inject a service into another service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.69,
          "end": 39.3,
          "en": "which is something we'll do later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.3,
          "end": 43.23,
          "en": "the element injector is not really an option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.23,
          "end": 46.83,
          "en": "because those other services aren't elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.83,
          "end": 49.35,
          "en": "and therefore don't try to get values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.35,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "from that element injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "But for components and directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 56.88,
          "en": "the element injector is part of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.88,
          "end": 61.11,
          "en": "that injector tree Angular looks up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.11,
          "end": 65.4,
          "en": "So back in the code, if I comment out @Injectable again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.4,
          "end": 68.66,
          "en": "we could also provide that tasks service with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.66,
          "end": 73.26,
          "en": "of the element injector to our tasks component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.26,
          "end": 75.93,
          "en": "and all related components by going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 79.023,
          "en": "to the tasks component ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.023,
          "end": 83.78999999999999,
          "en": "And then there we can add a provider's array to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.78999999999999,
          "end": 87.333,
          "en": "that component decorator configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.221,
          "end": 92.497,
          "en": "And the idea behind this provider's array here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.497,
          "end": 96.27000000000001,
          "en": "that it allows you to set up values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.27000000000001,
          "end": 98.94,
          "en": "that should be injectable, that are tied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.94,
          "end": 102.723,
          "en": "to the element injector that belongs to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.56,
          "end": 107.7,
          "en": "Now all child components, so all components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.7,
          "end": 111.63,
          "en": "and elements used in the template of the tasks component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.63,
          "end": 116.506,
          "en": "will also have access to that element injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.506,
          "end": 119.4,
          "en": "But other components, like the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.4,
          "end": 122.602,
          "en": "for example, wouldn't have access to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.602,
          "end": 125.94,
          "en": "So the service is then in the end restricted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.94,
          "end": 129.269,
          "en": "to that part of your component tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 129.269,
          "end": 132.54,
          "en": "And there also is another important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 134.253,
          "en": "to which I'll get back later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.09,
          "end": 139.02,
          "en": "So we can also add our tasks service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.02,
          "end": 142.03,
          "en": "to this provider's array in the tasks component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.43,
          "end": 147.69,
          "en": "so that all the task related components, so app new task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.69,
          "end": 151.23,
          "en": "and the tasks list have access to that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 151.23,
          "end": 153.18,
          "en": "And they will have access to one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.18,
          "end": 156.122,
          "en": "and the same instance of that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.122,
          "end": 159.66,
          "en": "If we would provide the tasks service inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 159.66,
          "end": 162.48,
          "en": "of the tasks list component, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 162.48,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "it would get access to a different instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 168.72,
          "en": "of the service than the new task component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.72,
          "end": 170.493,
          "en": "But like this, it will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.423,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "If we save that, we therefore can again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 180.53,
          "en": "add our tasks, change the status, filter and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.5,
          "end": 183.663,
          "en": "That all still works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 188.61,
          "en": "But that's how we can use the element injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 188.61,
          "end": 191.34,
          "en": "There is something important you must understand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.34,
          "end": 194.643,
          "en": "and know about that element injector though.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
